      },
      "classification": "finite-example",
      "adaptations": [
        "Use the explicit-rule array variant: retain all seven rules, six rewrites, six source checks, push/pop, and run 5. Commutativity, associativity, folding, and zero identity remain explicit rewrites.",
        "Represent Neq tuples with constructors equated to Present; require the witness in every relation consumer. Preserve the active contradiction condition using Conflict and a check after each run, before pop.",
        "Alpha-rename globals and qualify primitive operations for ours; translate negative equality checks to fail/check for egglog. Include positive guard validation and a missing-read-guard negative control."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Contradictions reject at explicit checkpoints rather than at the original immediate panic; this changes error timing.",
        "Private witnesses preserve tested tuple membership only. Merging asserted roots into Present does not preserve general relation-row identity.",
        "This finite example uses explicit binary rewrite matching; no native-AC equivalence or performance claim is made."
      ],
