    {
      "id": "list",
      "source": {
        "path": "tests/web-demo/list.egg",
        "sha256": "0db0bffbf91fdd80d9f28c1fa62c51931c5fe98d8ac4e2e7c9b404113a79135d",
        "url": "https://github.com/egraphs-good/egglog/blob/593df10e1465904e8b7a3dc85d8ef3976842b509/tests/web-demo/list.egg",
        "vendored_path": "fixtures/core/list/upstream.egg"
      },
      "classification": "finite-example",
      "adaptations": [
        "Retain both primitive-result tables, both demand relations, all six rules, append/set rewrites, all source input lists, and all five source checks. Replace source saturation with a bounded 10000-round computation run.",
        "Keep n > 0 on recursive demand and i > 0 on update. The final get-propagation rule deliberately has no n > 0 guard; its n > MIN guard only prevents undefined query subtraction.",
        "Use boxed scalar outputs and private Present witnesses for demand/definedness. Separate validation rules check definedness and conflicting no-merge outputs without advancing computation.",
        "Bind stored primitive keys and test their computed-key equality. Preserve partial-query definedness guards before arithmetic; alpha-rename globals and qualify primitives in ours.",
        "Validation seeds a negative-index tail value and checks its propagation; the control checks that a zero-index tail/head collision is rejected rather than hidden by an added positive-index guard."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "The 10000-round bound reached saturation for the audited finite source; it is not a translation of arbitrary unbounded schedules.",
        "Conflicts reject after computation at a validation checkpoint, changing native no-merge error timing. Cyclic conflicting inputs are not represented by these selected cases.",
        "The boxed no-merge interface does not establish mutable merge-new/min/max tables, arbitrary scalar-box unions, or general relation-row identity.",
        "Additional validation phases, boxes, and computed-key joins change the measured workload; no native-table performance equivalence is claimed."
      ],
