        "Retain seeds fib(0)=0 and fib(1)=1, forward recurrence with query x+1 and write x+2, the seven computation rounds, and the source fib(7)=13 check.",
        "Use boxed scalar outputs and private Present witnesses for demand/definedness. Separate validation rules check definedness and conflicting no-merge outputs without advancing computation.",
        "Bind stored primitive keys and test their computed-key equality. Preserve partial-query definedness guards before arithmetic; alpha-rename globals and qualify primitives in ours.",
        "The x < MAX query guard preserves undefined x+1 as no match; arithmetic in rule heads remains checked and must still fail if undefined. The rounds-5 validation checks both the populated frontier and the missing next key; the wrong-answer control must fail."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Validation does not advance the recurrence but delays conflict detection until a checkpoint.",
        "This is forward primitive-table population, not recursive constructor-demand Fibonacci. Only the finite source and listed controls are classified here.",
